WEBVTT

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.400
Parasaurolophus was a dinosaur that thrived

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:09.070
on what is now the North American
continent during the Cretaceous period.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.070
They say it could grow to ten meters in height,

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:15.610
and its weight exceeded four tons.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:19.660
It had a uniquely-shaped crest that extended backwards from its head.

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:24.580
The crest contained tubes that connected to its nostrils,

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.420
which, it is said, produced a sound similar to an oboe.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:29.550
Today's point of interest!

00:02:00.550 --> 00:02:02.720
I hate my weakness...

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.970
I want...

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:07.350
I want power!

00:02:08.810 --> 00:02:10.100
It won't open!

00:02:10.100 --> 00:02:12.610
You make a mountain out of every molehill, don't you?

00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:29.750
Here. It's open.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.750
Oh! Thank you, Botan!

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.710
Yes! Carbonated drinks! Yes!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.930
Well, she doesn't usually get to make use of it,

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.930
but it's a big help at times like this, huh?

00:02:41.930 --> 00:02:43.720
Botan's "super-strong" setting!

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:44.850
Don't call it my "setting."

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:47.890
Well, if you really feel like you never get to use it,

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.980
you should teach us some simple self-defense techniques!

00:02:51.230 --> 00:02:53.610
I want to learn some techniques, too!

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.650
Good idea.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.440
You're cute, so it'd be a good thing for you to know.

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:02.490
Something bothers me about the way you said that...

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:03.280
Right!

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.080
Then, I'll teach you the secrets of Hagizuki-ryuu!

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.870
That's not necessary.

00:03:07.870 --> 00:03:10.710
Okay, Sakura, can you be my opponent?

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:12.120
Leave it to me!

00:03:13.330 --> 00:03:15.710
I happened to bring my "Suspicious Person Kit" today.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:16.880
Why?!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:17.960
Well?

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:20.050
Do I look like a suspicious person?

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.430
Yes, you're totally suspicious.

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:24.640
A level of suspicious we rarely see in this day and age.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.560
I'd report you to the police.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.390
You'd even make children cry!

00:03:31.730 --> 00:03:33.520
Why are you sulking?

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:35.110
You're a real pain.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.230
Okay, Sakura!

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.900
Attack me however you like!

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.370
I'm going to send you joke faxes!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.870
Why is she attacking with psychological warfare?

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:51.870
I'll put fermented soy beans in your mailbox.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:54.210
These are all really underhanded attacks!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:57.380
Okay, I'll put socks I wore for two weeks straight

00:03:57.380 --> 00:03:59.260
over the summer in your mailbox.

00:03:59.800 --> 00:04:01.720
Enough. Just attack me directly.

00:04:02.010 --> 00:04:04.260
If you don't, I can't use any self-defense techniques.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.140
Okay, then!

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.760
I'm gonna lick the back of your knees!

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.930
Oh no!

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:13.520
I can't lick them with this mask in the way!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.100
What an idiot.

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:17.770
Roll!

00:04:17.770 --> 00:04:21.990
If you're attacked from the front, take the attacker's arm like this.

00:04:22.530 --> 00:04:24.740
In this situation, the pinky finger is key.

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:29.370
Keep the pinky, the attacker's weak point, held down.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:34.710
Then just twist that arm outwards.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:36.880
Of course, I won't do that now, since it's dangerous.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:40.630
Wow... And then I wouldn't be able to move?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:42.800
Nope. You'd burst.

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:48.140
Hidebu!

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:52.270
We can't use that.

00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:54.890
Botan.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:04:57.770
What do you mean by "burst"?

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.020
Well, you see...

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.570
Hello.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:05.740
It's me.

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:08.030
Yes, it's...

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:09.280
the usual.

00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:10.530
The usual?

00:05:14.410 --> 00:05:15.750
Is that...

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:30.050
Yes. Please take care of it.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:30.430
She did that right at the beginning.
Yes. Please take care of it.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.760
She did that right at the beginning.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:35.140
No, it's not as bad as last time.
You shouldn't need the marble block.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.770
Ah... the usual, huh?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.150
She defeated the suspicious person!

00:05:44.150 --> 00:05:46.780
Botan sure is strong.

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.370
I want to be just like Botani!

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:51.280
You can't.

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.240
Huh?

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:55.370
You mustn't become like Botan.

00:05:55.700 --> 00:05:57.120
O-Okay...

00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:00.500
You absolutely mustn't.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.250
Don't worry.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.920
I'm sure she won't.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:06.880
It's true that I'm strong.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:10.640
It takes no effort for me to make a normal person burst at the seams.

00:06:11.640 --> 00:06:16.480
But that is not where true strength lies.

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:20.520
The true strength that people seek

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:23.730
lies not in the body, but in the mind.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:25.820
What do you mean by "burst"?

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:29.950
So you undergo mental training too, Botan?

00:06:31.990 --> 00:06:32.660
Yes.

00:06:33.280 --> 00:06:34.790
For instance...

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:40.080
I am unfazed when someone reads my diary from middle school!

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.830
Wh-What?

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.460
Impossible!

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:48.010
Middle school diaries are full of
immature urges, reckless ignorance,

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:50.880
unrealistic ideals, bitter love stories...

00:06:50.880 --> 00:06:53.970
It all comes together in a Pandora's Box of chaos!

00:06:54.810 --> 00:06:56.890
They say that, the day a stranger opens it,

00:06:56.890 --> 00:06:59.940
even a seasoned master will writhe in agony

00:06:59.940 --> 00:07:02.270
and suffer a mental breakdown!

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:03.860
Where do they say that?

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.110
Th-That's true...

00:07:07.570 --> 00:07:10.070
Even for a practitioner of the peerless Hagizuki-ryuu,

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.240
such a claim is hard to fathom...

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.240
Why are you trembling?

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.030
Incidentally, I have it here.

00:07:16.030 --> 00:07:17.620
You carry it around with you?!

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.250
Th-This is...

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:23.580
The title even has daggers bookending it!

00:07:24.130 --> 00:07:29.010
A normal person would faint from the
agony of someone else just seeing that!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:31.510
You can get that symbol just by typing in "Dagger."

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:37.510
By the way...

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.480
Is this note even necessary?

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.270
Is it an old personal web page or something?

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:45.480
Is it really okay to read this?

00:07:45.480 --> 00:07:47.400
Yes, it's no problem.

00:07:56.030 --> 00:07:58.160
Sakura!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:07:59.500
What happened?!

00:07:59.500 --> 00:08:01.540
Was it a forbidden magic spell?

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:04.370
P-Parasaurolophus...

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:07.750
A Parasaurolophus's horn is stabbing me...

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:09.550
She's even rambling incoherently!

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.380
Bzzt!

00:08:12.010 --> 00:08:16.680
Just what is written in that diary?

00:08:20.810 --> 00:08:23.140
I'm... going to read it.

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.810
I'll read it aloud so you all can hear.

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:34.490
Okay. I'll read this part.

00:08:35.280 --> 00:08:39.740
"July 12th. I am broken glass."

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.120
"No one will come near me."

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:45.620
"Anyone who touches me gets hurt."

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:47.460
"And yet..."

00:08:48.750 --> 00:08:51.840
"When bathed in light, I will surely glitter."

00:08:53.970 --> 00:08:55.680
Natsuki!

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.680
I'm glass, huh?

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:03.270
That's a pretty interesting metaphor I came up with.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:08.400
"When bathed in light, I will surely glitter."

00:09:09.480 --> 00:09:12.070
I guess there was a time when I believed that...

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.820
She took no damage from having that read aloud in front of her?

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.450
Natsuki, here's some water.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:20.910
This... This is Hagizuki-ryuu!

00:09:21.990 --> 00:09:25.790
After that, I started high school

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:27.960
and met a light by the name of Sakura.

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:34.130
Botan really is amazing.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:36.880
She can write things that affect people this much.

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:43.600
Maybe I should keep a diary, too!

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.940
You shouldn't look directly at the sun.

00:09:49.940 --> 00:09:52.770
Use special glasses or a solar filter to do so!

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:02.030
Rat-tat-tat-tat-tat!

00:10:02.030 --> 00:10:03.410
Now we're in a battle!

00:10:04.410 --> 00:10:06.120
Pinching the legs to fire?

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.210
That takes me back!

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:10.670
I used to modify them, too.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.050
I tried attaching a long barrel, for instance.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.920
I even attached a magazine made from a plastic bottle,

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:19.380
but it jammed so easily.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:21.300
There!

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.930
Karin, say "ah"!

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.220
Ah!

00:10:25.350 --> 00:10:26.730
How much are you going to spoil her?!

00:10:33.820 --> 00:10:35.030
How rude!

00:10:35.030 --> 00:10:37.030
I'm not spoiling her.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.320
I was just peeling an orange for her.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:42.030
What high school student can't peel their own oranges?!

00:10:42.030 --> 00:10:44.330
But it's dangerous if you get orange juice in your eyes.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.370
My eyes! It hurts!

00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.950
You're just being overprotective!

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.080
To be honest, Claire,

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:52.250
I think you've been spoiling Karin too much lately.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:56.170
Karin, I put more lead in
your mechanical pencil for you.

00:10:56.170 --> 00:10:58.670
Oh, thank you!

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:00.180
That's exactly what I'm talking about!

00:11:00.180 --> 00:11:03.260
But, if the lead were to stab her in the eye—

00:11:03.260 --> 00:11:04.350
It won't!

00:11:04.350 --> 00:11:06.180
What if you spoil her so much,

00:11:06.180 --> 00:11:09.890
she becomes the kind of person who can't do anything for herself?

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:12.400
Could you take responsibility

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:14.520
for looking after Karin for the rest of your life?

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.110
Yes, I could.

00:11:17.980 --> 00:11:19.280
You could?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:21.820
It's true.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:26.160
If there is one thing that could drive me to sin,

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:27.790
it would be...

00:11:29.160 --> 00:11:32.120
Karin's cuteness.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:44.800
Enough of that joke already!

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.600
And don't draw Karin floating in
the sky like someone who's dead!

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:51.270
How nice for you, Karin.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:53.600
You've won at life.

00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:56.440
Oh no!

00:11:56.440 --> 00:11:58.190
The club president has given up on something!

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.570
If you give up, Karin is done for!

00:12:00.990 --> 00:12:05.410
Well, it's true that spoiling someone all the time won't help them.

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:08.580
She just gave good advice!
Her diary is still ridiculous, though.

00:12:08.950 --> 00:12:10.830
It's a good idea to be strict sometimes.

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.380
They say even the lion drops
his cub into a valley of carrots.

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:18.040
That must be rough for a carnivore.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:19.840
Or maybe it was a valley of discipline...

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.920
Bzzt!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:23.800
I feel bad for the cub!

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:25.550
You should discipline it yourself!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:26.720
Okay.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.470
Karin, come with me for a moment.

00:12:29.470 --> 00:12:30.470
Huh?

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:33.560
Now, Karin!

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:36.520
Climb this stairway with your own two legs!

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:38.150
How low are you setting the bar?!

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:39.400
No way...

00:12:39.730 --> 00:12:41.900
I have to climb all these stairs by myself?

00:12:41.900 --> 00:12:42.570
What?

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:44.780
Why are you just going with the flow?

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:47.410
But there are at least ten steps...

00:12:47.410 --> 00:12:50.450
You walked up them at lunch while humming to yourself!

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:51.080
Hey...

00:12:51.450 --> 00:12:54.290
Botan, this might be a bit much...

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:56.120
Not her, too!

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:58.340
You can climb a staircase hopping on one leg!

00:12:58.340 --> 00:12:59.170
Wait a minute.

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.510
I'll call my bodyguard.

00:13:01.510 --> 00:13:02.920
He'll climb it for you.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.010
You're missing the point completely!

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.720
Then, I'll call a helicopter...

00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.180
How high are you planning on taking her?!

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:11.770
If you can't walk up, you may
climb on your hands and knees.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.060
She gave up on making her use her own two legs!

00:13:31.280 --> 00:13:32.290
I see.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:33.910
Very well.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:59.900
All you have to do is hold on to me.

00:14:01.900 --> 00:14:03.440
Botan...

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:13.450
What do you mean by "burst"?

00:14:19.920 --> 00:14:22.210
Give the seals some love, too!

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:43.150
7:30, huh?

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:50.610
Waking up early on a Sunday
makes me feel like I'm losing out.

00:15:00.710 --> 00:15:01.630
Right.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:03.210
I'll do some warm-up exercises.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:27.980
I guess it's lunchtime.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.510
Even in the pictures she uploads herself,

00:15:49.510 --> 00:15:50.760
she includes retorts.

00:15:50.760 --> 00:15:52.090
She's so dedicated.

00:15:57.100 --> 00:16:01.770
Karin's Feminine Appeal level is as high as ever.

00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:04.060
There.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.020
I've finished "liking" all the pictures that

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.690
my cute underclassman friends have uploaded.

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:13.610
Sakura... is uploading
nonsensical pictures again.

00:16:13.610 --> 00:16:16.990
I wish there was a "Die" button next to the "Like" button.

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:18.830
Huh?

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:22.460
I think this girl was in my third year class in middle school.

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:26.380
It's been a while...

00:16:26.790 --> 00:16:28.250
I wonder how she's doing.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.850
Whew!

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:38.050
Thank goodness!

00:16:38.050 --> 00:16:40.640
It's a good thing I've done mental training!

00:16:40.640 --> 00:16:43.770
A normal person would've had a mental
breakdown and died from seeing that.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:48.060
...and that's what happened yesterday.

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:51.570
Wow, it's been so long since I broke a punching bag!

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:57.490
Botan, you didn't have any friends
in your third year middle school class?

00:16:58.160 --> 00:16:59.580
Not just in my third year.

00:16:59.580 --> 00:17:04.160
Sakura is the first person I've
ever been able to call a friend.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.750
You've walked a seriously lonely road...

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:08.880
What?!

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:10.050
But why?!

00:17:10.050 --> 00:17:12.170
Botan is so nice!

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:15.800
I don't think it was that they didn't like her...

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:18.180
They were just afraid of her.

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:22.350
Botan unconsciously exudes a murderous aura, after all.

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:26.480
Normal people sense it instinctively and keep their distance.

00:17:26.480 --> 00:17:31.070
But I've never thought of
Botan as scary even once.

00:17:31.070 --> 00:17:34.820
That's because she was already with us when you met her!

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:37.740
When she's like this, you don't have to be afraid.

00:17:40.160 --> 00:17:42.040
If you'd met her in a situation like this,

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:44.000
she might have made a different impression.

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:48.170
I think I understand...

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:50.420
But then, Sakura,

00:17:50.420 --> 00:17:53.130
how did you get to be friends with Botan?

00:17:53.710 --> 00:17:54.550
What?

00:17:56.380 --> 00:17:59.970
After that, I started high school

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:02.470
and met a light by the name of Sakura.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:09.350
What on earth happened in their past?

00:18:10.270 --> 00:18:11.770
Before I met Sakura,

00:18:12.070 --> 00:18:13.940
I had spent my whole life alone.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:19.110
But that had its positives, too.

00:18:19.740 --> 00:18:24.370
Hagizuki-ryuu is closely tied to your mental strength.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:27.460
So the loneliness made my body stronger.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:30.960
Thanks to my training,

00:18:30.960 --> 00:18:33.500
when we were told to pair up in gym class,

00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:36.510
I got through it using afterimages made by high-speed motion.

00:18:37.420 --> 00:18:40.930
You wouldn't have needed to do that if you had friends...

00:18:41.800 --> 00:18:44.310
If any of you ever seriously tried to hit me,

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:46.930
I don't think it would even hurt me.

00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:48.100
Huh?

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:50.400
That can't be true!

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:52.560
Because... See?

00:18:52.560 --> 00:18:55.190
Your cheeks are as soft as anyone else's!

00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:55.940
Poke, poke!

00:18:56.360 --> 00:18:58.650
Well then, why don't you try, Sakura?

00:18:59.360 --> 00:19:01.070
Get serious.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:02.530
You asked for it!

00:19:04.450 --> 00:19:05.580
Don't you dare...

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:08.450
regret saying that now!

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:12.170
Why do you look happier after every hit?

00:19:12.330 --> 00:19:14.630
D-Damn!

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.460
It's really not affecting her!

00:19:16.460 --> 00:19:17.210
Well,

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:20.300
that last hit would've done some damage, so I'm glad it didn't!

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:21.760
But why?!

00:19:22.510 --> 00:19:24.390
If you hit a diamond with a feather,

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.220
do you think it would hurt it?

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:30.390
Didn't you say you were glass?

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:32.850
I hate my weakness...

00:19:33.690 --> 00:19:35.110
I want...

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:37.530
I want power!

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:40.490
Stop reusing footage to fill up airtime.

00:19:40.490 --> 00:19:41.280
Oh!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:43.280
Wait.

00:19:43.280 --> 00:19:48.160
She said that Hagizuki-ryuu was
closely tied to your mental strength.

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:50.000
Which means...

00:19:52.120 --> 00:19:53.880
Karin, come here a minute!

00:19:54.080 --> 00:19:55.000
Yes?

00:19:57.590 --> 00:19:58.460
What?

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.380
But that would...

00:20:00.380 --> 00:20:02.590
It's fine. Just do it like I told you.

00:20:02.590 --> 00:20:03.760
Hey, now.

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:05.930
Karin may have a high Feminine Appeal level,

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:07.720
but it won't make her hit harder.

00:20:09.350 --> 00:20:11.350
We'll see about that.

00:20:11.680 --> 00:20:13.310
Doumyouji Sakura...

00:20:14.270 --> 00:20:16.810
She's hit on a truly terrifying idea.

00:20:17.150 --> 00:20:20.240
At this rate, Botan won't stand a chance!

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.240
I don't really understand, but I'll give it a try.

00:20:23.400 --> 00:20:24.280
Go for it!

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:25.450
Give it your best shot!

00:20:28.700 --> 00:20:29.870
Whenever you're ready.

00:20:31.040 --> 00:20:32.750
Botan...

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:34.870
I hate you!

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:40.090
Botan, I hate you!

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:42.260
I hate you!

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:50.470
I'm sorry I'm late.

00:20:53.100 --> 00:20:55.520
What's going on, everyone?

00:22:45.880 --> 00:22:46.590
This is Botan.

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:48.970
The sand tiger shark has to eat

00:22:48.970 --> 00:22:51.550
its siblings in the mother's womb in order to be born.

00:22:51.550 --> 00:22:53.510
The battle starts before it's even born!

00:22:57.730 --> 00:22:58.730
And two more!
